 "notes": {
  "bHow": {
   "fill": "blue",
   "page": "balanced",
   "size": 24,
   "text": "What changed, and why\n\n• Today opens with three big numbers (waiting on you, on my desk, filed) instead of a paragraph.\n• One coloured block per screen, for the thing that matters most. On Today it is the blue \"waiting on you\" block: blue still only means waiting on you.\n• Every item has a mark (email, question, web, watch) so you can tell things apart without reading.\n• Progress is drawn (3/5 and a bar), prices get a small chart, and work shows a small picture of what the agent saw.\n• One line per item. A second line appears only for risk, like \"Can't be undone\".\n• Secondary actions became round icon buttons with a short label.\n• Speaking is a full page: your words in large type, a live voice level, one button to hand it off.\n• Night appearance: warm ink with a soft desk-lamp light at the top.\n\nPress Play on Today and click through. Hold the blue button on \"For your signature\".",
   "w": 520,
   "x": -640,
   "y": 0
  },
  "bRefs": {
   "fill": "orange",
   "page": "balanced",
   "size": 24,
   "text": "From the references: ideas, not looks\n\nTaken: big numbers as anchors, blocks of different sizes for rhythm, icons that replace words, round action buttons, speaking as a first-class screen, a soft light in the dark.\n\nLeft behind: pastel tiles, blue glow backgrounds, glass bars, emoji and photos in greetings, a dark top with a white sheet, floating toolbars.\n\nEverything stays in Ledger's paper and ink, serif and signatures. Full notes in docs/design/references/README.md.",
   "w": 520,
   "x": -640,
   "y": 900
  },
  "bTitle": {
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 2740,
   "page": "balanced",
   "text": "Rebalanced: glance first, read second",
   "w": 240,
   "x": 0,
   "y": -300
  },
